{"id": "EUVD-2026-103843", "enisaUuid": "09c2b1bb-f5b1-3311-ac52-294a8d96323f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: typec: ucsi: glink: fix use-after-free of ucsi on remove\n\nThe pmic_glink client is released by the devres cleanup, which runs\nafter pmic_glink_ucsi_remove() has returned, so its notification\ncallbacks can queue work until then. Work that runs after\nucsi_unregister() has been called touches freed state: it dereferences\nthe connector array that ucsi_unregister() freed, or registers and\nunregisters the instance a second time.\n\nDisable both work items with disable_work_sync() before unregistering,\nand unregister only if the instance is still registered.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:25:11", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/432b58cd959e594909a581b4974396cdbc9d4ca1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/41934f92e7a54d4080ac0b17aacc83224946785c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee8577de01c6b6c7dd1d76b52242c54d37a989f4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/63b269ec537dc0fd26d0bd64872c26860d108c9d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98758", "GHSA-hvv7-vw9m-6v98"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1aaf1da5-7e99-3344-a8af-fe453eeac373", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "410717c1-98bd-3a6f-9489-e130f2661ffc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "617312fa-7755-354d-b597-aff9ddc51750", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "62b5412b1f4afab27d8df90ddcabb8e1e11a00ad <432b58cd959e594909a581b4974396cdbc9d4ca1"}, {"id": "777fdf2a-ebec-3be6-892e-a9910f4f1d68", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4"}, {"id": "81c9096d-4d2f-33b1-8cbc-80d7c264efd7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "90b3cee2-52ae-38d2-9636-4753007f6b9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "62b5412b1f4afab27d8df90ddcabb8e1e11a00ad <41934f92e7a54d4080ac0b17aacc83224946785c"}, {"id": "b46a7d35-5ed9-3249-875e-99fd66d2cf37", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "d2c43055-3059-34ce-8d78-b9e7f804d50a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "62b5412b1f4afab27d8df90ddcabb8e1e11a00ad <ee8577de01c6b6c7dd1d76b52242c54d37a989f4"}, {"id": "e823b55b-9016-3869-8709-fc1a46c09df6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "fda38395-046c-3ed1-bdfb-94fdc32d221b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "62b5412b1f4afab27d8df90ddcabb8e1e11a00ad <63b269ec537dc0fd26d0bd64872c26860d108c9d"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d24b8192-bc93-393d-93c8-9a10f4de9400", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}